    {
      "version_number": "1.0.5",
      "run_date": "2026-05-02T02:59:59.833385",
      "changelog": "- Updated all Maton API endpoints from gateway.maton.ai and ctrl.maton.ai to api.maton.ai for consistency.\n- Clarified instructions for specifying a Salesforce connection via the Maton-Connection header, emphasizing its use when multiple connections exist.\n- Added a new \"Security & Permissions\" section requiring explicit user approval before any write operations (create, update, delete).\n- Removed LICENSE.txt file."
    },
    {
      "version_number": "1.0.6",
      "run_date": "2026-05-03T03:42:13.922530",
      "changelog": "- Added strong security guidance: treat the API key as secret, rotate if exposed, and revoke unused Salesforce connections promptly.\n- Updated description and usage to emphasize least-privilege OAuth, sandbox use for risky actions, and always verifying connection ID before requests.\n- Clarified that only supported/documented endpoint paths should be used.\n- Instructions now require explicit user confirmation with details before any write or batch operation; added steps to confirm record and intended impact.\n- Emphasized defaulting to read-only actions and increased caution on all composite/batch operations."
    },
    {
      "version_number": "1.0.7",
      "run_date": "2026-05-09T03:44:10.833903",
      "changelog": "- Adds CLI and Homebrew installation instructions for Maton CLI, expanding usage options.\n- Updates API examples and references from Salesforce API version v59.0 to v63.0.\n- Documents direct CLI commands for common actions (SOQL queries, connections) alongside Python and HTTP examples.\n- Clarifies connection management and explicit connection selection, now with CLI examples.\n- Improves authentication instructions by including CLI login/interactive login commands.\n- No functional/API changes to the underlying integration; documentation update only."
    }
  ]
